 blacks go home pup and tell your  mother that the Lord of Storm's end is  not some dog that she can whistle up but  need to set against her foes realizing  that he is ill-prepared for this  negotiation luceris attempts to leave  before he is able to depart however  aemond demands that luceras cut out his  own eye to make up for the wound lucerus  had inflicted on aemond in their youth  however boros doesn't particularly care  for this Bluster and allows luceres to  leave taking to his young dragon air ax  who is greatly unsettled by the ongoing  intense storm lucerus begins to fly back  to Dragonstone soon however he realizes  that Ament is in Pursuit with vegar the  largest and most fearsome dragon in  Westeros Eamonn taunts luceris from  atompa's Dragon still demanding his eye  but both children have trouble  controlling their dragons on account of  them being untested Dragon Riders  as eamon's pursuit of luceris becomes  more and more dire lucerus's dragon air  ax is visibly shaken and both dragons  appear to be letting their Primal  instincts take over despite the protests  of both Riders as the hunter vegar size  is incredibly apparent though this  doesn't stop air acts from blasting the  ancient dragon with fire this in turn  causes vegar to release its full Fury  upon both aerax and luceris and in an  instant both dragon and Rider are killed  with a ravenous bite from vegar  this comes as a surprise to aim it who  realizes that his actions will have  deadly consequences as shocking as this  scene was for viewers this scene  actually has far more Nuance than what  was presented in firing blood in the  grand scheme of things this scene is  considered a defining moment in the  conflict known as the dance of dragons  and several different variations of the  story are told regarding what happened  but all agreed upon one thing luceris  and Eric's were tragically undermatched  against aemond and vegar and while you  see that amend is clearly disturbed by  what happened in the show that's not how  it goes down in the book this is on  account of the nature of the way Fire  and Blood is written as a kind of  historical document with unreliable  narrators the book portrays the fight as  one-sided and very much intentional with  aemond motivated primarily by Revenge  there are several stories told about the  aftermath of the fight with some saying  that aerax's head washed ashore others  saying that both luceris and erax were  swallowed hole and one suggesting that  luceris actually survived but suffered  from permanent Amnesia either way  luceris is never found  this change in House of the Dragon makes  for a much more Dynamic story which is  important considering this moment Sparks  the Targaryen Civil War in Westeros  although rhaenyra didn't want to strike  the first blow she was given her wish  albeit at a terrible price to see amond  realize his actions will have disastrous  consequences clearly shines a new light  on the story and it'll be interesting to  see how he'll report the outcome to his  family in an interview with variety  series co-creator Ryan Condell was asked  about why they decided to make luceras's  death an accident and not intentional he  clarified that even though it is  presented as an accident Eamonn still  jumped onto his dragon and chased his  nephew so it isn't as clear-cut as a  simple mistake kondel then explained how  history itself is messy and how the  historians and storytellers of Westeros  couldn't actually know what was going  through eamon's head he added this is a  war of many cuts that lead to a really  really bloody wound it adds complexity  and Nuance to the character that's  potentially interesting discussing the  future of eamon's story condolated  there's lots of Runway to go on with  aemond as a character and the story of  the dance this is his first act as a  dragon rider and a warrior and it's gone  very wrong now what happens as a result  and how does he respond those are the  questions I'm interested in as a  dramatist ultimately this departure from  The Source material definitely adds yet  another layer to the upcoming conflict  and the way both signs will respond and  shape the history of Westeros  foreign
 

